<section class="shell band">
  <h1>Our LPC Associates</h1>
  <p class="hero-lede">Finding Balance Counseling works as a supervised practice. Alongside
  Reem Glasco, LPC-S, a group of <strong>LPC Associates</strong> sees clients under her
  supervision, which means the same clinical lineage at <strong>lower fees and sooner
  availability</strong>. Most work online across Texas; one also sees clients in person in
  Austin. Every associate offers a free consultation first.</p>
</section>

<section class="band band--night">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>At a glance</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <caption>All associates are LPC Associates in Texas, supervised by Reem Glasco, LPC-S.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Associate</th><th>Works with</th><th>Fee, 50 minutes</th><th>Sliding scale</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for a in associates %}
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/therapy/associates/{{ a.slug }}/">{{ a.name }}</a></td>
            <td>{{ a.glance }}</td>
            <td>{{ a.feeTable }}</td>
            <td>{{ a.sliding }}</td>
          </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>For comparison, a 50-minute session with <a href="/therapy/">Reem</a> is $240, and her
    caseload is small because of her supervision and consultation work. The associates are not
    the budget option so much as the available one.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band">
  <h2>The associates</h2>

  <div class="cards cards--roster">
    {%- for a in associates %}
    <div>
      <img src="/assets/img/associates/{{ a.photo }}" width="{{ a.photoW }}"
       height="{{ a.photoH }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
       alt="{{ a.name }}, {{ a.credential }}.">
      <div>
        <h3>{{ a.name }}, {{ a.credential }}</h3>
        <p>{{ a.summary }}</p>
        <p>
          {%- if a.feeIndividual %}<strong>{{ a.fee }}</strong>{% if a.feeSlidingFrom %},
          {{ a.sliding | lower }}{% endif %}. {{ a.consult }}.
          {%- else %}Fees are discussed in the free consultation.{% endif %}<br>
          {%- if a.email %}<a href="mailto:{{ a.email }}">{{ a.email }}</a>{% endif %}
          {%- if a.email and a.phone %} &middot; {% endif %}
          {%- if a.phone %}{{ a.phone }}{% endif %}
          {%- if not a.email and a.website %}<a href="https://{{ a.website }}"
           rel="noopener">{{ a.website }}</a>{% endif %}
        </p>
        <p><a href="/therapy/associates/{{ a.slug }}/">More about {{ a.name | first_name }}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

</section>

<section class="band band--sand">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2>How to choose</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>Availability and fee decide it more often than specialty does. If you already know
        what you are bringing, the table above points at one or two people. If you do not, say
        what is going on in a few sentences through the contact page and you will be pointed at
        the right fit rather than left to guess.</p>
        <p>You can also write to an associate directly. Every one of them offers a free
        consultation first, which exists precisely so that neither of you commits to a poor
        match.</p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Ask which associate fits</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>What supervision means for you</h3>
        <p>An LPC Associate in Texas is fully qualified and licensed to practice, and is
        completing the 3,000 supervised hours the state requires before full licensure. Their
        work is reviewed every month by a Council-approved supervisor, which here means Reem.</p>
        <p>In practice that means a second experienced clinician is thinking about your case
        alongside the person in the room. <a href="/texas-lpc-licensure/">The licensure guide
        explains the requirement in full.</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about seeing an associate</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>What is an LPC Associate?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>A counselor who has finished a master's degree, passed the required exams and holds a
      Texas LPC Associate license, and is completing 3,000 supervised hours toward full
      licensure. It is a license to practice, not a trainee status, and the work is supervised
      monthly by a Council-approved supervisor.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How much does it cost to see an associate?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>{{ associateStats.individualRange }} for a 50-minute individual session depending on
      the associate, and {{ associateStats.couplesRange }} for couples or family sessions.
      {{ associateStats.slidingCount }} of the {{ associateStats.count }} hold a limited number
      of sliding-scale places, starting at {{ associateStats.slidingFrom }}. Sessions with Reem
      herself are $240.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do the associates have sooner availability than Reem?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Usually yes, and that is the main reason to start here. Reem keeps a small therapy
      caseload alongside supervising associates and consulting on EMDR, so her openings are
      limited and often waitlisted.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is therapy with an associate as good?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>It is different rather than lesser. An associate is earlier in their career and brings
      more open attention and a supervisor reviewing the work each month. Reem has been in
      practice since {{ site.licensedSince }}, with a particular depth in developmental trauma
      and stalled EMDR. For complex
      developmental trauma she is the better fit; for most other presentations an associate is a
      good one.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I see an associate in person?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Sheila Singh sees clients in person in Austin as well as by telehealth. The others work
      online across Texas. Trail walk and equine sessions are offered by Reem rather than the
      associates.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do associates offer couples or family therapy?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes. Natasha Mahesh sees couples and families at $150 for 50 minutes, and Sheila Singh
      sees couples at $165. Reem's own caseload is individual therapy.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
    {% include "partials/faq-more.njk" %}
{% include "partials/crisis-note.njk" %}
</section>

